-- CA_0178_dispute_wrong_committee_links_active_rows.sql
-- Mark 680 WRONG campaign-finance committee links as 'disputed'. Each sits on an ACTIVE politician row, at
-- research_status = 'needs_research', and was made by matching a surname (or a token that is not the row's surname at
-- all) against committee names, so the committee belongs to someone else. Follow-up to CA_0174 and CA_0177, which did
-- the same for deactivated placeholder rows; the CA_0177 review found that four of its la_socrata committees were also
-- linked, the same way, to active rows (Erik Miller, Deborah L. Christian, Hector M. Guzman).
--
-- SCOPE: every 'needs_research' link on an active politician row -- 1,886 links on 431 rows (1,852 cal_access, 34
-- la_socrata), measured 2026-09-23. All 1,886 were reviewed. 680 are disputed here; 1,206 are left as they are:
--   682 whose committee name carries the row's own given name as well as the surname (out of scope: this file only
--       judges surname-only links; several are leads, see the CSV), and
--   524 surname-only links that nothing shows to be someone else's (the honest status for them is still
--       'needs_research'; 160 of those name another office type but no other place, which is not evidence against a
--       real officeholder, who may have run for it).
-- The disputed links were made by confirm-cal-access.ts (642 cal_access), discover-by-jurisdiction.ts (3),
-- seed-la-county-officials-from-discovery.ts (1) and relink-socrata-skipped.ts (34 la_socrata, flagged by sweep 1664);
-- 633 of the cal_access ones were demoted to needs_research by migration 1792, 13 arrived there later. 578 on the
-- surname alone, 102 on a token that is not the row's surname ("DE" of De Leon Sanchez, the surname of a different
-- person the row was once merged with, a word such as "LAW" or "PARKS").
--
-- Per-link table (all 1,886), with official committee name, filer area code, status, LA City Ethics candidate, basis,
-- reason and any lead:
--   data/roster-audits/2026-09-23-active-row-committee-links-CA_0178.csv
--
-- EVIDENCE (fetched 2026-09-23):
--   * Cal-Access committee detail page for all 1,852 cal_access filers (official name, filer phone, status). Control
--     filer 1414018 returned "NEWSOM FOR CALIFORNIA GOVERNOR 2022" at the start and at the end of the run. One filer
--     (1420401) returned an error page; it is judged on its stored name only.
--   * LA City Ethics contributions dataset (data.lacity.org m6g2-gc6c) cand_name / seat_desc for the 34 la_socrata
--     links and for every cal_access filer id it knows (63 of them): e.g. 1262901 "Miller for Mayor" = Addie Miller,
--     1438114 "Christian L. Guzman for City Council 2022" = Christian Guzman (LA CD15), 1254386 / 1275192 "Hahn for
--     Mayor 2005" = James Hahn, 1268665 = Sylvia Luna Nerio.
--   * Filer phones were compared within each row: 12 surname-only committees share a personal filer phone (one that
--     serves at most three surnames, so not a treasurer's) with a committee on the same row that this file places
--     elsewhere. Phones are NOT written anywhere: politician_sources is public-read, so reasons carry the area code only.
--
-- BASIS (the CSV column 'basis'):
--   A  450  the committee names another person, or the matched token is a place ("PARK" in Menlo Park, "ROSA" in
--              Santa Rosa, "HILL" in Morgan Hill, San Gabriel, Lathrop, Peralta), a word ("LAW", "PARKS", "GOLDEN"),
--              the particle "DE", or someone else's GIVEN name ("SCOTT" Peters, "ANTHONY" Phan, "DOUGLAS" Strehl,
--              "MARSHALL" Tuck). Includes all 34 la_socrata links: LA City Ethics names a different candidate for each.
--   B  123  the committee is for another named place or district (Beverly Hills, Chula Vista, Hollister, Galt, the
--              Cosumnes CSD, the Anaheim City SD ...), or it is a committee OPPOSING the surname, or a recall / ballot
--              committee -- not the row's own campaign committee.
--   C  107  the filer evidence places it elsewhere: 95 are for another office type than any the row holds, with a
--              filer area code outside the Los Angeles region (916 excluded: Sacramento treasurers serve many
--              campaigns), and nothing ties them to the row; 12 share a personal filer phone as above.
--   These are active, real officeholders, so the bar is higher than on the placeholder rows of CA_0174/CA_0177: a
--   committee for another OFFICE is not, by itself, disputed here (Adrin Nazarian's Assembly committees are his own).
--   A same-office committee with a far area code is not disputed either (it may still be the row's).
--
-- LEFT ALONE: the 1,206 links above. 83 of the 524 surname-only ones sit on 25 active rows that hold no seat and no
-- race (e.g. Caroline Menjivar, Tony Strickland, Phil Brock -- all three flagged incumbents with no office_terms
-- row), so "another place" cannot be judged for them; only named-person evidence was used on such rows.
--
-- NOT IN SCOPE -- the committee-named rows. Every cal_access committee here is ALSO linked to an inactive
-- essentials.politicians row whose full_name IS the committee name (source 'cal_access_discovery', 76,330 rows for
-- 64,242 filers; 12,088 filers have two such rows). They are a committee directory made by
-- discover-cal-access-candidates.ts, each with one orphan office (no chamber, no district, mostly no title) and one
-- open office_terms row from the 1459 backfill; nothing else references them, they carry no money or ingestion runs,
-- and every read path skips them (is_active = false, see CC_0101). Their 76,330 self-links are not false attributions
-- to a person, so they are not disputed. Retiring them is a separate, ruled change (the Indiana precedent is
-- CC_0101-CC_0104).
--
-- WHY 'disputed' AND NOT DELETE OR RE-POINT: 'disputed' is the admin API's own value for a wrong link
-- (campaignFinanceAdmin.ts), as in CA_0166, CA_0174 and CA_0177. Every read path and the ingestion scheduler require
-- research_status = 'confirmed' and nothing reads 'needs_research' (migration 1792), so all 680 links were already
-- inert: disputing them changes the record so the next research pass does not confirm them. No money moves: the 680
-- links carry 0 contributions and 0 contribution_summary_agg rows. Nothing is deleted: 157 ingestion_runs (on 50 of
-- the links, from before migration 1792) keep their source.
--
-- NOTES FORMAT: 667 of the 680 notes are "<json> | UNVERIFIED (migration 1792 ...)" or "<json> | sweep 1664: ..." text
-- and get the " | "-joined suffix those migrations used: " | DISPUTED by CA_0178 (2026-09-23): <reason>". 13 (Robert
-- Luna's) are plain JSON objects and get disputed_by / disputed_reason keys merged in (IS JSON OBJECT branch, as in
-- CA_0174). politician_sources is public-read, so no reason carries a phone number.
--
-- OVERLAP CHECKED: CA_0166, CA_0174 and CA_0177 work on inactive placeholder rows; none of their links is here. No
-- migration on master or on any unmerged branch writes these 680 links. The Guzman re-link lead from CA_0177 is its
-- own file, CA_0179.
--
-- No migration runner exists; this file records SQL applied by hand (pure DML).
-- STATUS: APPLIED to prod 2026-09-23 (operator approval: Chris Andrews). The dry run was repeated right before the
-- apply; verified after on row counts: 680 disputed with the marker, 1,206 needs_research on active rows, confirmed
-- (1,340) and not_applicable (3,574) on active rows unchanged.
--
-- ROLLBACK:
--   UPDATE transparent_motivations.politician_sources
--      SET research_status = 'needs_research',
--          notes = CASE WHEN notes IS JSON OBJECT THEN (notes::jsonb - 'disputed_by' - 'disputed_reason')::text
--                       ELSE left(notes, strpos(notes, ' | DISPUTED by CA_0178 (2026-09-23): ') - 1) END
--    WHERE research_status = 'disputed' AND strpos(notes, 'CA_0178 (2026-09-23)') > 0;
-- IDEMPOTENT: the update is guarded on each link's prior status; a re-run is a no-op and every gate still passes.

BEGIN;

CREATE TEMP TABLE _link (id uuid PRIMARY KEY, politician_id uuid, source_system text, external_id text,
                         prior_status text, committee text, reason text) ON COMMIT DROP;
